    <string name="help_button">Help</string>
    <string name="help_intro">
        <![CDATA[The <B>DoC Outdoors</B> app is intended to provide simple and
        straightforward listings of the various New Zealand Department of
        Conservation assets that are maintained for public leisure. As well as
        Campsites, Huts, and Tracks, there\'s a list of Alerts, which brings to
        light any current closures and/or hazards on DoC sites. These alerts can
        be updated automatically within the app, either daily or weekly &#8230;
        refer to the Settings section below for more on Auto Update.]]></string>
        <string name="help_lists">
        <![CDATA[When you view a list for the <I>first</I> time, the app will
        automatically download those items from DoC servers. Be patient while the
        list downloads &#8230; for the best experience, please ensure that the
        download completes before switching to another app or activity.]]></string>
        <string name="help_items">
        <![CDATA[When the list appears, you can then view individual items,
        and optionally download an image, plus further info for that asset
        (images not for the available for alerts). Also, in the case of
        Tracks, the map coordinates for the complete track.]]></string>
        <string name="help_maps">
        <![CDATA[On that note, you can view one or all items on a map by using
        the Map Overview icon on the toolbar, or the individual Place icon next to
        each item\'s location. If no map coordinates are available for that item,
        the icon will simply be <FONT color="#888888">greyed out</FONT>.]]></string>
        <string name="help_settings_auto_upd">
        <![CDATA[In the Settings section of the app, you can enable Auto Update for
        the Alerts if desired. However, this is <I>only</I> available if the Alerts
        are filtered by region. Updates can be carried out either Daily or Weekly,
        <I>without</I> your having to do anything. To customise the update process,
        there are options for allowing the use of Mobile Data, allowing Notifications
        (subject to permission on Android 13+ devices), and the option to Wait until
        the Device is Charging, i.e. overnight, when the device is idle. Once each of
        these options has been configured, remember to tap the Save button. A bonus with
        the Auto Update feature is that <I>affected assets</I> info is also downloaded,
        bypassing the need for you to download these manually, per item.]]></string>
        <string name="help_settings_filtering">
        <![CDATA[Also in the Settings section, you\'ll find the option to <B>filter</B>
        any list by region. Alerts can also be <I>sorted</I> by name if desired, although
        the default is to show the newest first. There\'s the option to filter Campsites
        and Huts by <B>bookable</B>, i.e. whether or not you can book them ahead of your
        trip. Another filter available is <I>just</I> for Campsites and Tracks: <B>dog
        access</B>. Options for filtering include:<UL><LI>Dogs on a leash</LI><LI>Dogs
        with a DOC permit</LI><LI>Dogs allowed</LI><LI>and, No dogs</LI></UL>]]></string>
    <string name="help_settings_extras">
        <![CDATA[For just Campsites, Huts and Tracks, there are options to <I>also</I>
        download related extras, <I>if</I> filtered by region. This saves you having to do
        this manually per item, plus it enables <B>Advanced Search</B> (see Manage Search
        icon at left) so, instead of searching only by name, you can also search within
        item descriptions, and for Campsites and Huts, within facilities too.]]></string>
    <string name="help_settings_tracks">
        <![CDATA[For just <I>single</I> Track maps, you can choose whether or
        not to zoom in automatically on a newly downloaded track.]]></string>
    <string name="help_settings_maps">
        <![CDATA[Two final settings (for <I>all</I> maps) give you the option to include
        <I>your</I> own location on maps (subject to permissions); plus selection of
        the map <I>type</I>, whether Normal (default) or Satellite view.]]></string>
    <string name="help_title">Help &amp; Intro | Settings</string>
    <string name="help_subtitle">Help and Introduction</string>

